{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '32,46p' '/home/rafa/Documents/zmoot/Rafa/00 Inbox/ETF inbox.md'\"","aggregated_output":"### Candidate: Who are the 5 largest ETF lead market makers? (research 2026-11-06; Q3 target 2026-09-30)\n\n**Awaiting Rafa's approval. Historical quarter-end ranking unresolved.** The official files available today are current snapshots, not archived September 30 assignments. The table ranks **assigned ETP securities across the retrieved US program lists**, not a verified ETF-only universe or trading-market share. No historical rank is inferred.\n\n| Rank by assignments | Exchange-normalized firm | NYSE Arca file | Nasdaq DLP | Cboe BZX LMM | Total assignments |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | Jane Street | 624 | 245 | 254 | 1,123 |\n| 2 | Virtu | 562 | 171 | 121 | 854 |\n| 3 | GTS | 281 | 158 | 391 | 830 |\n| 4 | Susquehanna | 311 | 219 | 211 | 741 |\n| 5 | Citadel | 358 | 151 | 151 | 660 |\n\n**Official sources / dates:** [NYSE ETF resources](https://www.nyse.com/products/exchange-traded-products/exchange-traded-funds) links the [current Arca workbook](https://www.nyse.com/publicdocs/nyse/markets/nyse-arca/NYSE_Arca_Equities_LMM_Current.xlsx); [Nasdaq ETF definitions](https://www.nasdaqtrader.com/trader.aspx?id=etf_definitions); [Cboe LMM securities](https://www.cboe.com/us/equities/listings/trade_on_cboe/lmm/securities/). All retrieved **2026-11-06**. NYSE has one sheet, `LMM Details 2026-10-05`, and workbook modified metadata `2026-10-05T18:37:49Z`; use **October 5 sheet date**, not September 30. No internal effective date was established for Nasdaq or Cboe. Retrieval is the observation date, not proof every record changed that day. The NYSE resources page calls it “NYSE Listed ETPs”; the workbook filename is Arca. Coverage of NYSE proper's DMM assignments has **not** been established; this is not an all-NYSE-venues ranking.\n\n**Method:** parse the NYSE XLSX with Python zipfile/XML and the other two HTML tables; deduplicate symbol/firm within each venue. NYSE: 2,742 rows with symbols/assignment text → 2,728 unique assignments excluding 13 “No LMM” rows and one duplicate symbol/firm. Nasdaq: 1,279 unique DLP assignments; exclude Market Quality Supporters. Cboe: 1,674 unique symbol/firm rows including one test account → 1,673 after removing that account. Short exchange labels are grouped by named firm (Jane Street, Virtu, GTS, Susquehanna, Citadel), not by a claimed legal-entity identifier. Totals count exchange assignments, not globally deduplicated funds; listing-transfer overlaps have not been reconciled. An ETF-only classification join remains necessary. **AUM ranking not computed:** no cheap, reliable identifier/date-matched quarter-end join was obtained. Assets supported by an LMM would measure client-fund size, not the firm's own AUM or quoting volume.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The **November 6, 2026 retrieval** ranks firms by combined assignments:\n\n| Rank | Firm | Assignments |\n|---|---|---:|\n| 1 | Jane Street | 1,123 |\n| 2 | Virtu | 854 |\n| 3 | GTS | 830 |\n| 4 | Susquehanna | 741 |\n| 5 | Citadel | 660 |\n\nSources: [NYSE Arca workbook](https://www.nyse.com/publicdocs/nyse/markets/nyse-arca/NYSE_Arca_Equities_LMM_Current.xlsx), [Nasdaq DLP](https://www.nasdaqtrader.com/trader.aspx?id=etf_definitions), [Cboe BZX LMM](https://www.cboe.com/us/equities/listings/trade_on_cboe/lmm/securities/).\n\n**Date limits:** NYSE’s sheet is dated **October 5, 2026**; Nasdaq/Cboe effective dates were not established. Retrieval does not establish September 30 holdings or assignments.\n\n**Universe limits:** Counts cover assigned **ETP securities**, not verified ETF-only coverage. Symbol/firm pairs are deduplicated within venues, not across venues; firm labels are normalized. Excludes Nasdaq Market Quality Supporters, Cboe’s test account and “No LMM.” NYSE proper’s DMM coverage is unestablished.\n\n**Worth knowing:** This measures assignment counts—not AUM, trading share or a global ranking."}}
